&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a detail-oriented and analytically minded finance professional to join the Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis team at Squarepoint, a leading quantitative investment manager. The individual should have a solid understanding of financial data management and reconciliation, with experience working across finance systems and a confidence in ensuring data is accurate, well-structured, and fit for purpose. The role will focus on improving the quality and integrity of contract and financial data, as well as owning the tracking and loading of leasehold improvement spend, with outputs that directly improve the reliability of FP&amp;amp;A forecasting, reporting, and invoice processing across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role suited to someone who takes pride in data accuracy, enjoys investigating and resolving financial misalignments, and is motivated by the opportunity to create tangible and lasting improvements in data quality and process. The role offers real visibility across the finance function and the chance to work with a broad range of stakeholders, making a meaningful impact on the quality of information that underpins decision-making across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing actual ledger postings against contract data to identify and resolve misalignments in financial attributions, ensuring contracts are correctly tagged at source across all relevant dimensions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing contract run rates against contracted values, engaging with business owners to understand and document variances and revise contract values where necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing inactive contracts to assess whether they should remain active, reducing noise in the data and improving forecast reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with the Technology team to explore opportunities to improve recording of contract data in a way that enables more granular and accurate reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with external partners to ensure the monthly leasehold improvement trackers are completed accurately and capture all required information for FP&amp;amp;A and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loading leasehold improvement data into the FP&amp;amp;A forecasting platform on a monthly basis, ensuring it reconciles correctly and is available for stakeholder reporting and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience in a finance, FP&amp;amp;A, or financial control role, with a solid understanding of how financial data flows between systems and feeds into reporting and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reconciling financial data across systems, with the ability to identify root causes of misalignments and work with stakeholders to resolve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with the ability to build and maintain professional relationships across all levels of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High personal standards, strong attention to detail and a desire to exceed expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An independent mindset, with the confidence to challenge existing processes and propose improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A well-structured, proactive work ethic with the ability to work under pressure and manage deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curious mindset and a natural interest in understanding the wider business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to technology and motivated to find ways to streamline and improve processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLM tools in either a professional or personal context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a CRM or contract management system, and experience using a financial planning or EPM tool, would be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data visualisation, including graphs and dashboards, would be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p data-start=&quot;153&quot; data-end=&quot;664&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;153&quot; data-end=&quot;191&quot;&gt;Qube Research &amp;amp; Technologies (QRT)&lt;/strong&gt; is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology and data-driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology, and trading expertise has shaped our collaborative mindset, which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high-quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;666&quot; data-end=&quot;966&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You will join a procurement function that supports technology infrastructure, cloud services and strategic supplier relationships across the firm. The role focuses on transforming complex operational, financial and infrastructure data into actionable insights that support procurement decisions, capacity planning, supplier management and investment strategy. You will work closely with procurement, finance, engineering and operations stakeholders to develop reporting, forecasting and analytics capabilities across a growing technology estate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your future role within QRT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract, cleanse and integrate data from cloud platforms, procurement systems, infrastructure management tools and financial systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain dashboards and reporting for procurement, infrastructure, finance and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse infrastructure utilisation, asset lifecycle trends, capacity planning metrics and technology refresh programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine cloud consumption, procurement, financial and operational datasets to provide business insights and decision support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse cloud, colocation and infrastructure costs to support investment planning and optimisation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop forecasting models for infrastructure demand, supplier commitments and hardware procurement planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and operations teams to provide insight into server utilisation, storage growth, network capacity and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate opportunities to improve infrastructure performance, resiliency and cost effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop KPI frameworks and operational metrics for cloud services, infrastructure assets and operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve automated reporting, analytics workflows and data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present findings and recommendations to technical and non technical stakeholders, including senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic decision making through reporting on supplier commitments, infrastructure investment and capacity planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your present skillset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Data Analytics, Computer Science, Engineering or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 or more years of experience in data analysis within procurement, infrastructure, asset management, finance or technology operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of AWS reporting, cloud financial management and cloud consumption analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analysing infrastructure assets, capacity planning, hardware lifecycle management and technology refresh programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills and strong SQL expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Python for analytics, automation and data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Tableau or similar visualisation and reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret complex datasets and generate actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with experience presenting to senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ERP platforms and procurement systems such as SAP or Coupa is beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure management, asset management or data centre management platforms is advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cloud computing, storage architectures and infrastructure best practices is beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building automated data pipelines, ETL processes and enterprise reporting solutions is advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of FinOps principles, supplier commitment management and infrastructure investment analysis is beneficial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3073&quot; data-end=&quot;3385&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Qube Research &amp;amp; Technologies (QRT) is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology and data driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology, and trading expertise has shaped QRT’s collaborative mindset which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high-quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an exceptional Data Analyst to join our team. In this role you will collaborate closely with Researchers, Analysts, and Engineering teams to ensure the timely delivery, quality, and effective use of financial data across the firm&#39;s research and trading platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your future role within QRT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Python-based data pipelines to ingest, transform, validate, and load external financial datasets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard new datasets by understanding vendor documentation, mapping data fields, defining schemas, performing historical backfills, and deploying production-ready data feeds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own assigned datasets throughout their lifecycle, monitoring data pipelines, resolving data delivery issues, and improving reliability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve data quality issues such as missing data, duplicates, stale values, outliers, and identifier or calendar inconsistencies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external data vendors to resolve delivery issues, clarify data definitions, and manage format or coverage changes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document datasets, transformation logic, and operational processes to support long-term maintainability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with researchers, analysts, and engineers to deliver reliable datasets that meet business requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your present skillset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in Financial Data, Market Data, Data Engineering, Data Operations, or a similar data-focused role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or master&#39;s degree in a quantitative discipline such as Mathematics, Physics or Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced programming experience in Python, including proficiency with data handling libraries such as Pandas and NumPy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with structured and semi-structured data such as CSV, JSON, XML, Parquet, APIs, or vendor data feeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with financial market data, reference data, pricing, fundamentals, corporate actions, ESG, or alternative datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience investigating data quality issues and reconciling datasets against independent sources.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Git and modern development practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills with the ability to collaborate effectively across global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brex is the intelligent finance platform that enables companies to spend smarter and move faster in more than 200 markets. By combining global corporate cards and banking with intuitive spend management, bill pay, and travel software, Brex enables founders and finance teams to accelerate operations, gain real-time visibility, and control spend effortlessly. Brex’s AI-native automation and world-class service eliminate manual expense and accounting tasks for customers so they can focus on what matters most. Tens of thousands of the world&#39;s best companies run on Brex, including DoorDash, Coinbase, Robinhood, Zoom, Plaid, Reddit, and SeatGeek.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Brex allows you to push your limits, challenge the status quo, and collaborate with some of the brightest minds in the industry. We’re committed to building a diverse team and inclusive culture and believe your potential should only be limited by how big you can dream. We make this a reality by empowering you with the tools, resources, and support you need to grow your career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Data at Brex&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data organization develops insights, models, and data infrastructure for teams across Brex, including Sales, Marketing, Product, Engineering, and Operations. Our Data Scientists, Analysts, and Engineers work together to make data—and insights derived from data—a core asset across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Data Analyst II (DA), you will play a central role in enhancing the operational tracking and reporting capabilities of different business teams across Brex. You will work closely with Data Scientists, Data Engineers, and partner teams to drive meaningful insights for the business through visualizations, self-service tools, and ad-hoc analyses. This is a high-impact role in a fast-paced fintech environment where your work will directly influence strategic decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you’ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in our New York office. We are a hybrid environment that combines the energy and connections of being in the office with the benefits and flexibility of working from home. We currently require a minimum of three coordinated days in the office per week, Monday, Wednesday and Thursday. As a perk, we also have up to four weeks per year of fully remote work!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply data visualization and storytelling skills in creating business intelligence solutions (such as Looker and/or Hex dashboards) that enable actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform ad-hoc analyses and deep dives to investigate business questions, surface trends, and provide data-driven recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop self-service data tools and processes that empower business stakeholders to independently monitor the performance and health of their respective areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Data Scientists and Data Engineers to identify data sources, enable data pipelines, and support the development of analytical data models that operationalize reports and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain rigorous data quality checks to ensure the integrity and robustness of datasets used across dashboards, reports, and analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with various departments—including Sales, Operations, Product, and Finance—to understand their data needs and deliver tailored analyses and reporting that support strategic planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the automation of recurring analyses and reporting workflows using Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in data analytics or a related role in a professional setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience working directly with Sales, Operations, Product, or equivalent business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in SQL to manipulate data and perform complex analyses (CTEs, window functions, joins across large datasets).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python for data analysis, automation, or scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with business intelligence and data visualization tools (Looker, Hex, Tableau, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative and analytical skills with a demonstrated ability to translate data into business insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with stakeholders across different functions and levels of technical fluency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with generative AI and LLM-based tools (Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot) to perform and accelerate analyses, automated reporting, and build self-service data tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud data platforms (e.g., Snowflake, BigQuery, Databricks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with dbt for data modeling and transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to data pipeline orchestration tools (e.g., Airflow).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, financial services, or payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with evolving priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $93,600 - $117,000. However, the starting base pay will depend on a number of factors including the candidate’s location, skills, experience, market demands, and internal pay parity. Depending on the position offered, equity and other forms of compensation may be provided as part of a total compensation package.&lt;/p&gt;
